Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||12-31-2000||12:32 AM||||<BR>My friend has a '88 GT W/ 80k miles on the new engine the problem is that it has no ass to it at all (a Contour beat him) there is a loug turbo like wine coming from the driver side intake vent we un hooked the intake at the throttle body and the noise was louder than ever, the car also idles at 2000 RPM steady. I belive it is a Vac. leak at one of the intake manifold gaskets, but before we tear into the engine has any one had this problem before?<P>P.S. the car is completly stock||||reg||5
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||12-31-2000||12:39 AM||||I forgot the sound is there at all RPM but is loudest when cruiseing at part throttle and is not audible at WOT||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||12-31-2000||01:16 AM||||If you have wine coming from the intake vent I would check the air cleaner for grapes!   ||||reg||12
Z||000003||Will||12-31-2000||09:33 AM||||The idle air passage may have come unseated. I did this once and the car acted like it had an enormous vacuum leak. The idle air tube is ~1/2" diameter and connects to the back of the throttle body directly beneath the throat of the intake manifold. It seats in an o-ring hole and does not go in very far. If that is your problem, you can re seat it by reaching under the throttle body and putting it back in place.||||reg||1
